/**
 * K3 implant Ā· W1-T1 Ā· security boundary barrel + registration.
 *
 * COMPONENT TRIPLE (verification_kernel.md Ā§4.5.10)
 * - Reason to exist : one registration point means one place to prove the declaration surface and
 *                     the enforcement surface are the same set.
 * - Axiom binding   : Axiom 5 (environment layer), Axiom 1 (in-kernel Python runs with user rights).
 * - Deprecation     : the barrel is an implementation convenience and may be replaced; the
 *                     `installK3SecurityBoundary` contract (probe ā†?allowlist ā†?guard ā†?ledger)
 *                     is not deprecable.
 *
 * UNINSTALLABILITY (a K3 requirement, not a nicety): every K3 implant must be removable on its own
 * without breaking the Prime main loop. This module therefore only ADDS files under `src/k3/` and
 * exposes pure functions; deleting `src/k3/security/` plus the two call sites in
 * `kernel/index.ts` (dispatch assertion) and `agent-session.ts` (construction wrapping) restores
 * upstream behaviour exactly. Nothing here mutates upstream module state at import time.
 */

